<title>HONG KONG: HK Oct orders on hand fall six pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Oct orders on hand fall six pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said October orders-on-hand fell six percent in value on the year against a 11 percent drop in September.  </p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders-on-hand in October 1996 over October 1995 (* means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						   Oct 1996   Sept 1996</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey    -6	  -11</p>
<p> Wearing apparel				***	   -3*</p>
<p> Textiles					 ***	   -3</p>
<p> Electronic Products			  -12	  -21</p>
<p> Electrical products			   -3	   +1</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		   +5	   +2*</p>
<p> Plastic products			     -10	  -16</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		    -14	   -9</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
